    <section class="section-pad bg-light-custom" id="prep-tips" aria-labelledby="tips-heading">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row g-5">
                <div class="col-lg-6 fade-up">
                    <div class="eyebrow">Expert Advice</div>
                    <h2 class="section-title" id="tips-heading">How to Crack <span class="text-gold">CA Foundation in First Attempt</span></h2>
                    <div class="divider-gold ms-0"></div>
                    <p>Our faculty, who have coached over 17,500 students through CA Foundation, share their proven preparation strategy:</p>
                    <div class="tip-item"><div class="tip-num">1</div><div class="tip-content"><h6>Start Immediately After Class 12 Registration</h6><p>Register for CA Foundation with ICAI on the first eligible day and begin coaching without any gap. Time is your biggest asset.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="tip-item"><div class="tip-num">2</div><div class="tip-content"><h6>Master Accounting First</h6><p>Paper 1 (Accounting) is the highest-scoring and most predictable paper. Build a strong foundation here and it boosts your aggregate significantly.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="tip-item"><div class="tip-num">3</div><div class="tip-content"><h6>Practice QA Daily — Even 30 Minutes</h6><p>Quantitative Aptitude requires consistent daily practice, not marathon sessions. 30–45 minutes every day beats 5 hours once a week.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="tip-item"><div class="tip-num">4</div><div class="tip-content"><h6>Read Business Laws as Stories</h6><p>Each section of a law has a purpose and a context. Understanding why a law exists makes it infinitely easier to remember and apply in answers.</p></div></div>
                    <div class="tip-item"><div class="tip-num">5</div><div class="tip-content"><h6>Attempt All Mocks Under Exam Conditions</h6><p>Sit at a desk, set the timer, switch off your phone, and write on paper. Simulated exam conditions build the exact temperament needed on D-day.</p></div></div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 fade-up">
                    <div class="eyebrow">Avoid These Mistakes</div>
                    <h3 class="mb-4">Common Mistakes CA Foundation Students Make</h3>
                    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
                        <div class="feature-card p-3 h-auto" style="border-left:4px solid #DC2626">
                            <h6 style="color:#DC2626"><i class="fa fa-circle-xmark me-2"></i>Ignoring Paper 4 (Business Economics)</h6>
                            <p style="font-size:.85rem">Most students focus on Accounting and neglect Business Economics until the last week. This is a fatal mistake — Economics contributes 100 marks and needs continuous attention.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="feature-card p-3 h-auto" style="border-left:4px solid #DC2626">
                            <h6 style="color:#DC2626"><i class="fa fa-circle-xmark me-2"></i>Over-Relying on Shortcuts in MCQ Papers</h6>
                            <p style="font-size:.85rem">Papers 3 and 4 carry negative marking. Guessing without elimination strategy leads to net negative scores that can be exam-ending. Learn elimination techniques, not just shortcuts.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="feature-card p-3 h-auto" style="border-left:4px solid #DC2626">
                            <h6 style="color:#DC2626"><i class="fa fa-circle-xmark me-2"></i>Studying Without a Fixed Timetable</h6>
                            <p style="font-size:.85rem">Unstructured self-study without a proper schedule almost always results in neglected subjects and knowledge gaps that appear only on exam day. Follow a weekly study plan religiously.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="feature-card p-3 h-auto" style="border-left:4px solid #DC2626">
                            <h6 style="color:#DC2626"><i class="fa fa-circle-xmark me-2"></i>Skipping Revision to Cover New Content</h6>
                            <p style="font-size:.85rem">Finishing the entire syllabus without adequate revision is worse than covering 70% of the syllabus with thorough revision. Revision is where you convert knowledge into marks.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

