    <section class="section-pad bg-light-custom" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="text-center mb-5 fade-up">
                <div class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
                <h2 class="section-title" id="faq-heading">All Your Questions About <span class="text-gold">CA Foundation Coaching in Raipur</span> Answered</h2>
                <div class="divider-gold"></div>
                <p class="section-subtitle">Our counsellors have compiled the most common questions from parents and students about Excel Educational Institute and CA Foundation preparation.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4">
                <div class="col-lg-6">
                    <div class="accordion faq-accordion" id="faqLeft">

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">What is CA Foundation and who should join it?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">CA Foundation is the first level of the Chartered Accountancy course conducted by ICAI. Any student who has passed Class 12 from any stream — Commerce, Science, or Arts — can register for CA Foundation. There is no upper age limit. Commerce students with Accountancy background tend to find the transition smoother, but Science and Arts students who study diligently under proper guidance like that offered at Excel Educational Institute clear Foundation comfortably. CA Foundation is an excellent career choice for students who enjoy numbers, law, and finance and aspire to a high-paying, respected profession.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">What is the eligibility for CA Foundation 2025?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">To appear for CA Foundation, a student must have passed Class 12 (any board, any stream) from a recognised board. Students can also register for CA Foundation after passing Class 10, but they must complete the mandatory 4-month study period before they can appear in the exam. Registration must be done on or before January 1st for the May/June attempt and on or before July 1st for the November/December attempt. There is no age limit, no minimum percentage requirement in Class 12, and no restriction on the number of attempts.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">How many attempts does CA Foundation have per year?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">ICAI conducts CA Foundation twice a year — in May/June and in November/December. This means a student who registers on time gets two chances per year to clear the exam. There is no limit on the total number of attempts — students can appear as many times as needed until they clear all four papers. However, clearing in the first attempt saves valuable time and allows students to move to CA Intermediate faster. Excel Educational Institute's coaching program is specifically designed to maximise first-attempt pass rates, which currently stand at 78%+ among our students.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">Is negative marking in CA Foundation?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">Yes, negative marking applies specifically to Papers 3 and 4 of CA Foundation, which are MCQ-based. For every wrong answer, 0.25 marks (one-fourth of a mark) are deducted. There is no negative marking in Papers 1 and 2, which are descriptive/subjective papers. This is why Excel's coaching trains students extensively in elimination strategies for MCQ papers rather than wild guessing. Our mock tests mirror the negative marking pattern so students develop the exact risk-assessment mindset needed to score high in Papers 3 and 4 without losing marks unnecessarily.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">What is the passing criteria for CA Foundation?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">To pass CA Foundation, a student must satisfy two conditions simultaneously. First, they must score at least 40 marks out of 100 (40%) in each individual paper. Second, they must score an aggregate of at least 200 marks out of 400 (50%) across all four papers combined. If a student fails to meet either condition, they do not pass and must re-appear in all four papers in the next attempt. There is no group exemption concept in CA Foundation — all four papers are compulsory in every attempt. Our Excel coaching is structured to ensure students clear both conditions comfortably.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq6">How long does CA Foundation preparation take?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">ICAI mandates a minimum 4-month study period between CA Foundation registration and appearing in the exam. In practice, most students who join coaching after Class 12 study for 6–8 months before their first attempt. Students who join during Class 11 or early Class 12 have more time and can achieve significantly deeper preparation. At Excel Educational Institute, our standard CA Foundation batch runs for approximately 8–10 months, followed by revision sessions and the Model Test Series before the exam. Students who follow the full Excel program diligently are typically exam-ready well within this period.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq7">What subjects are there in CA Foundation 2025?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqLeft">
                                <div class="accordion-body">CA Foundation 2025 has four subjects: Paper 1 — Principles and Practice of Accounting (100 marks, subjective), Paper 2 — Business Laws (100 marks, subjective), Paper 3 — Quantitative Aptitude including Mathematics and Statistics (100 marks, objective/MCQ with negative marking), and Paper 4 — Business Economics (100 marks, objective/MCQ with negative marking). The total marks are 400. Each paper must be individually cleared with a minimum of 40 marks, and the aggregate must be at least 200 marks to be declared passed in CA Foundation.</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

