                        <div class="accordion-item fade-up">
                            <h3 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq29">What is the difference between CA Foundation, Intermediate, and Final?</button></h3>
                            <div id="faq29" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqRight2">
                                <div class="accordion-body">The CA course has three levels. CA Foundation is the entry-level exam (4 papers) that tests basic knowledge in Accounting, Laws, Maths, and Economics. After clearing Foundation, students move to CA Intermediate (8 papers across 2 groups) which covers advanced Accounting, Taxation (Direct and Indirect), Cost Management, Auditing, and Financial Management. During Intermediate, students also complete 3 years of articleship (practical training under a practising CA). After completing articleship and clearing CA Intermediate, students appear for CA Final (6 papers) — the most advanced level covering Advanced Accounting, Corporate Law, Strategic Management, Tax, and Financial Reporting. After clearing CA Final and completing articleship, a student becomes a qualified Chartered Accountant. Excel Educational Institute provides coaching for all three CA levels.</div>
